Ord. 2521-25
eBikes Amendment
 
ORDINANCE NO. __________
 
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING TITLE 6, CHAPTER 8 OF THE VILLAGE OF HAWTHORN WOODS
MUNICIPAL CODE REGARDING AGE RESTRICTIONS TO OPERATE ELECTRIC BICYCLES AND
ELECTRIC SCOOTERS
 
WHEREAS, the Village of Hawthorn Woods (“Village”) is a municipal corporation
lawfully organized and existing under the Constitution and laws of the State of
Illinois; and
 
WHEREAS, the Village is authorized to pass and enforce all ordinances, rules,
and regulations, proper or necessary, to carry into effect the powers granted
to the Village (65 ILCS 5/1-2-1; 65 ILCS 5/11-1-1) ; and
 
WHEREAS, the Village is authorized to regulate the use of Village streets and
other Village property, and traffic thereon, including electric bicycles and
electric scooters (65 ILCS 5/11-80-2; 65 ILCS 5/11-80-20; 625 ILCS 5/11-208(a)
(8); 625 ILCS 5/11-208(a)(15); 625 ILCS 5/11-1518(a)); and
 
WHEREAS, the corporate authorities of the Village desire to amend Title 6,
Chapter 8 of the Village of Hawthorn Woods Code of Ordinances (“Code”) to
modify age restrictions for persons operating electric scooters and electric
bicycles in the Village; and
 
WHEREAS, the corporate authorities of the Village find and determine that
amending Title 6, Chapter 8 of the Village Code, subject to the terms and
conditions of this Ordinance, is in the best interests of the health, safety,
and welfare of Village and its residents.
 
NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ORDAINED by the Mayor and Board of Trustees of the
Village of Hawthorn Woods, Lake County, Illinois, as follows:
 
SECTION 1. The foregoing recitals and findings of fact are incorporated as
though fully set forth in this Section 1.   
SECTION 2. Title 6, Chapter 8, Section 6-8-2 of the Village of Hawthorn Woods
Code of Ordinances is hereby amended, as follows (additions in bold and
underlined , deletions struck-through,  omitted language is not intended to be
amended):
6-8-2: OPERATIONAL RESTRICTIONS:
 
*         *         *
 
 B.   Restrictions Applicable To Low-Speed Electric Scooters:
      1.   No person under the age of 18 years shall operate an Low-Speed Ee
lectric Ss cooter , regardless of speed . No person shall operate an electric
scooter on any road with a posted speed limit greater than 35 miles per hour.
      2.   No person shall operate a low-speed electric scooter on any state
highway.
   C.   Restrictions Applicable To Low-Speed Electric Bicycles:
      1.   No person under the age of 16 shall operate a Class 3 low-speed
electric bicycle , regardless of speed .
2.   No person shall operate a low-speed electric bicycle on any sidewalk nor
upon any multi-modal walking path.
 
*         *         *
 
   SECTION 3. All ordinances, resolutions, and parts thereof in conflict with
this Ordinance are hereby repealed only to the extent they conflict with this
Ordinance
SECTION 4. If any part, subsection or clause of this Ordinance is deemed
unconstitutional, invalid or otherwise unenforceable by a court of competent
jurisdiction, the remaining sections, subsections, and clauses not affected
thereby shall remain fully valid and enforceable.
SECTION 5. This Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after its
passage and approval as provided by law.
 
 
